  "body": "This PR includes changs including: Adding Google Oauth sign up/in, database migrations including updated entities, clearly defined different role permissions, and general profile CRUD. This is a big change as previous main branch just was a baseline rails project with no features.\r\n\r\n## Associated User Stories\r\n- As an officer, I want new members to automatically appear on point sheet dashboard, because offiers do not want manual work.\r\n- As a potential member, I want to be able to go to the website, sign up (with TAMU email) and fill out a form with all my info (including when applying for PT school) and be registered into the system with access to everything because they will need to access member privleges if they join the org.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance Criteria\r\n### Non-members can easily find and open the recruitment form\r\n- Sunny: A visitor who isn't logged in clicks the clearly labeled \"Join\" button on the homepage, and the recruitment form opens.\r\n- Rainy: The form fails to load. The visitor sees a friendly error with an officer contact instead of a blank or dead page.\r\n### Only people with a TAMU email can apply\r\n- Sunny: An applicant enters a valid @tamu.edu email, and it is accepted.\r\n- Rainy: An applicant enters a non-TAMU email (e.g., Gmail). An error explains that a TAMU email is required, and the form is not submitted.\r\n### The form collects everything officers need, including PT school application info.\r\n- Sunny: An applicant fills in every required field (name, email, major, PT school details, etc.) and can submit.\r\n- Rainy: An applicant leaves a required field blank. An error names the missing field, nothing is sent, and the information already entered is kept.\r\n### Applicants get confirmation and officers receive the application\r\n- Sunny: The applicant clicks submit and sees a confirmation message. The application appears for officers (notification or list) and is saved in the system.\r\n- Rainy: The submission fails (e.g., connection or database issue). The applicant sees an error telling them to try again or contact an officer, and no partial or duplicate record is created.\r\n### New members can access member features after joining\r\n- Sunny: After registration (and approval, if required), the new member signs in with their TAMU Google account, sees a point total of 0, and can mark attendance.\r\n- Rainy: Someone with an email that is already registered submits the form again. They are told they already have an account, and no duplicate record is created. (If officer approval is required, someone signing in before approval sees a \"pending approval\" message and cannot access member features.)\r\n### New members appear on the point sheet dashboard automatically\r\n- Sunny: A new member completes registration (and approval, if required). Their name and TAMU email appear on the dashboard with 0 points, and no officer action is needed.\r\n- Rainy: The sync fails when a member registers. The member is not lost: they appear once the system recovers, or an officer is notified of the failure.\r\n\r\nDefinition of Done -\r\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied: \r\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented; \r\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes); \r\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.",
